          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4a2042275e7aea0ecf343b786dcfbca39e973467aebee1e7aa668ef8e67bffda:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4e1939c6da964cbc8d979a0237fa3615",
      "statement": "The `Embedder` protocol is a runtime-checkable Protocol with a single `encode(texts: Sequence[str]) -> list[list[float]]` method, so any duck-typed class that matches that signature plugs into `align_citations` and `PreparedCitationCorpus.from_sources`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/models/base.py#L1-L29",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9108e6d6e8e5f6e23dfae854123c5b44c081227e4299eade4958b4bf617c99b6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_894be4d02a76445c8dd1a48411fc0cbd",
      "statement": "`SentenceTransformerEmbedder` keeps a bounded LRU cache keyed on `(text, model_name)` (default cap 10,000 entries) so repeated encodings of the same text skip the underlying model.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/models/sbert_embedder.py#L1-L69",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:16e27e256314b6d2febdfdf4dc827e4469a8bc9491f414f8a860fc984efb5b86:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f532b3e98fc847e18c4b9d748afd7d55",
      "statement": "`EmbeddingIndex` stores the embedding matrix and precomputed L2 norms; `top_k` returns the top-k indices sorted by descending cosine similarity in the [-1, 1] range, and returns an empty list when the query vector has zero norm.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/models/embedding_index.py#L1-L78",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fcdd7412b55b640a7141f2f0d1d63f57a813eab7a2376a6701dae7a6cd817444:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_374a30518cec4901980cb5ab88be7700",
      "statement": "`CitationConfig` exposes `min_embedding_similarity` (default 0.3), `max_candidates_embedding` (default 200), `max_candidates_total` (default 400), and `CitationWeights.embedding` (default 0.5) to shape the embedder path; `permissive()` lowers the threshold to 0.25 and `fast()` drops `max_candidates_embedding` to 50.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/citation_config.py#L13-L182",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:23b6455ec04e3adfe7e683fced5a1d3a4f1a37691c864419b72f3d42c19451b4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_332a9c98219e454f9a2751d095e5264e",
      "statement": "Selected candidates are ranked by `max(embedding_score, lexical_score)` and capped by `max_candidates_total`, so a strong embedder hit on a non-seed window can still make the cut while keeping a stable ordering with the lexical seeds.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L1357-L1373",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6e9b2a144007f78dfb1e5d84fcb798493f5d28266a443fbb5140500b617a9414:"
        }
      ]
    }
